## Implementing an SVG Icon as a Clickable Element

To position an SVG icon to the right of an input field and make it clickable, you'll need to use a combination of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Here's a step-by-step guide to help you achieve this:

### HTML Structure

First, let's set up the basic HTML structure for your input field and SVG icon.

```html
<input type="text" id="input-field">
<svg id="reading-glass-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
  <!-- SVG icon content here -->
</svg>
```

### Styling the SVG Icon

Next, add CSS to position the SVG icon to the right of the input field. You can use flexbox or absolute positioning to achieve this.

```css
.input-container {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
}

#reading-glass-icon {
  margin-left: 10px;
}
```

### Making the SVG Icon Clickable

To make the SVG icon clickable, you'll need to add a `click` event listener to the SVG element using JavaScript. You can also use the `onclick` attribute on the SVG element, but the event listener approach is more flexible.

```javascript
const readingGlassIcon = document.getElementById('reading-glass-icon');

readingGlassIcon.addEventListener('click', function() {
  // Function to be called when the icon is clicked
  console.log('Icon clicked!');
  // Call your desired function here
  yourFunction();
});
```

### Full Example

Here's the complete example, including the input field, SVG icon, and event listener:

```html
<div class="input-container">
  <input type="text" id="input-field">
  <svg id="reading-glass-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
